{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["The reason for <b>And he removed that day the he-goats</b>: Scripture relates that Jacob made an unconditional request: remove from there every speckled and spotted among the goats. But Laban was concerned about the parent stock and separated the males and the females. He even separated the streaked ones that have a little white on their legs at the joint. And among the sheep he separated every one that had white in it and every dark one. Now if \"every one that had white in it\" is meant to say that among the he-goats and the goats he separated every one in which there was a white appearance, whether streaked or spotted, then \"and every dark one\" is an addition beyond the aforementioned appearances. The reason he added \"dark\" specifically in the wages of the sheep is because it is not in their nature to be multi-colored like the he-goats and the goats, and it is not in the nature of the goats to be dark among them."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "Reading ברוד as 'spotted/streaked' following Ramban's usage elsewhere; the term appears in Mishneh Hebrew for a dappled or grizzled pattern."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:37:12.452453798Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}